33,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The call-back trial showed a significant drop in readmissions for the elderly. It is a shame it was abandoned without a permanent structure.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"My findings are concerning. The booking system is blind to non-appointment work, and our physical space is already at a breaking point.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems my suspicions were correct. Our ""partnerships"" are often just polite agreements that crumble the moment a rota needs filling.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Yumi,,Oh no! I found out that the ward nurses are really struggling and using too many agency staff. We can't give them more work!,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The wind is shifting. I see that our budget has shrunk, and we are losing money if we move our care away from the hospital walls.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Yumi, if staffing is the bottleneck, we must choose a program that reduces long-term pressure rather than adding a new daily task.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Servas, if we cannot afford off-site work, we are forced to use the hospital. But the parking and rooms are already full. We cannot add more.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Which suggests we should avoid any program that relies on external surgeries or ""joint"" management. We need something self-contained and internal.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Yumi,,But the midwifery team actually has some extra time! Maybe we can find a way to help the ward nurses using the midwifery slack?,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"We must be careful. If we build a program that doesn't earn back its running costs, we are merely delaying a crisis.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"The call-back trial was internal and effective. If we can integrate that logic into a new program, we solve the outcome problem.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,Only if it doesn't require more rooms. Any program that increases the number of physical visits will cause the shuttle and parking to collapse.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I am quite tired of seeing ""joint ventures"" in our minutes that are actually just ""no one's responsibility."" Let's prioritize internal ownership.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"I just don't want the ward nurses to cry! If we pick a program that uses the midwifery staff's extra time, everyone will be smiling!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"Let us remember that a small, sustainable stream is better than a flood that dries up in a year. Revenue must match the ambition.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
