60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Candidate A mirrors the call-back trial's success. It targets readmissions directly and provides the evidence-based outcome we need.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Candidate A is the only viable option. It moves the activity off-site, avoiding our parking and room shortages, and doesn't clog the booking system.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Candidate B is a ""joint"" venture between departments—a recipe for a second-year collapse. Candidate D relies on outside providers, which is a bureaucratic nightmare.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Yumi,,I love Candidate B because it uses the midwifery team who have extra time! But Candidate A might be too hard on the ward nurses...,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"@Toshio, you say A is off-site. My findings show that off-site work earns no regional tariff. Candidate A would be a financial drain.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, the cost of a home visit is far lower than the cost of a readmitted elderly patient. The long-term savings are the real revenue.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"Financials aside, we cannot physically fit Candidate C. A ""dedicated space"" for a rehab unit is a luxury we simply do not have.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"I must agree with Asuka. Candidate A is internally managed. It avoids the ""joint"" failure of B and the ""external"" failure of D.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"If Candidate A is just visits, maybe the midwifery staff can help with the coordination? I want to make sure the ward nurses aren't stressed!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"Savings are not the same as income. However, if Candidate B is on-site, it earns tariffs. But is it sustainable for the staff?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,Candidate B is a luxury; Candidate A is a necessity for patient health. We cannot ignore the readmission data.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I cannot support B or C. The booking system is already failing; adding more scheduled consultations will only make the blindness worse.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Candidate B's ""joint delivery"" is a red flag. Who owns the budget? Who manages the rota? It will fall apart by next year.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I'll vote for Candidate B because the midwifery team is ready to help! It's the only way to not put more pressure on the tired nurses!,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"I see the wisdom in A's outcomes, but the lack of tariff is a grave concern. Yet, B's joint structure is indeed a fragile foundation.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,Let us choose the program that actually helps the patients. Candidate A is the only one with a proven track record here.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Toshio,,It is the only one that doesn't break the hospital's physical capacity. I am voting for A.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,Logic dictates we choose the path of least structural resistance. Candidate A is self-contained and effective.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Yumi,,"I still worry about the nurses, but if everyone else thinks A is the best, I'll try to help them make it work!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Servas,,"In the end, the health of the patient is the highest profit. If we manage the costs carefully, Candidate A is the most virtuous path.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
